  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed terraces to the front due to their siting and scale would result in an undue overlooking and unacceptable loss of privacy in relation to both adjoining properties. Furthermore, the proposed rear terrace at the top level due to its excessive scale and siting and the existing relatively small separation distances, would result in an unacceptable increase in noise levels in relation to both adjoining properties. As such, the proposed terraces would harm the residential amenities of the occupants of the adjoining properties. The proposal is therefore contrary to policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "Given the proposed roof form, extend of metal cladding and the overall design that would also accelerate the increase in mass and bulk, the proposal would appear as a dominant and intrusive addition that would not be in-keeping with the surrounding area causing harm to the character and appearance of the host dwelling and the Kingston Hill/Coombe Hill Strategic Area of Special Character, contrary to Policies DM10, DM12 of the Core Strategy (2012), Policies D3 and HC1 of the London Plan (2021) and Paragraph 135 of the NPPF (2024)."
